From: Korri Cemu investigation
Subject: [PATCH] ir3: finish late algebraic lowering after lowering imul

Problem: normal algebraic after ir3_nir_lower_imul recovers fmulz from
its abs-min lowering. A single late pass fuses fmulz + fadd to fmadz,
but does not revisit the replacement for abs-min lowering. Instruction
selection cannot emit fmadz. Iterate this final late pass to a fixed point,
just as ir3_nir_lower_variant already does.

Evidence: BotW vertex shader, Adreno 740, Mesa 26.2.3; pipeline BLAKE3
026211ce39d10e5e02021680ebff7da347ac4ee27a5064daeacd045d15efb127.
The unhandled 32-bit nir_op_fmadz enters ir3_context_error, then crashes
in ralloc_free. The single final late pass is the only late-algebraic
call in ir3 that does not run to a fixed point.

Upstream-status: Not submitted; local candidate for Mesa 26.2.x and main.
See mesa-26.2-ir3-fmadz.upstream.md for reproduction and validation status.
---
--- a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_context.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_context.c
@@ -93,10 +93,17 @@
       needs_late_alg = true;
    }
 
-   /* nir_opt_algebraic() above would have unfused our ffmas, re-fuse them. */
+   /* nir_opt_algebraic() above would have unfused our multiply-adds and
+    * recovered fmulz from its abs-min lowering.  Iterate to a fixed point:
+    * re-fusing fmulz + fadd can create fmadz, which needs another late pass
+    * to lower it before instruction selection.
+    */
    if (needs_late_alg) {
-      NIR_PASS(progress, ctx->s, nir_opt_algebraic_late);
-      NIR_PASS(progress, ctx->s, nir_opt_dce);
+      do {
+         progress = false;
+         NIR_PASS(progress, ctx->s, nir_opt_algebraic_late);
+         NIR_PASS(_, ctx->s, nir_opt_dce);
+      } while (progress);
    }
 
    /* This must run after the last nir_opt_algebraic or it gets undone. */
